Q1. What is the Singleton Design Pattern?
Why do we need it?

Interview Ready Answer

Singleton is a Creational Design Pattern
that ensures

• A class has only one instance.
• It provides a global point of access
  to that instance.

------------------------------------------------------------

Why do we need Singleton?

We use Singleton when only one object
should exist throughout the application.

Benefits

• Prevents unnecessary object creation.
• Saves Memory.
• Maintains a single shared state.
• Ensures consistency.
• Improves resource management.

------------------------------------------------------------

Real-Life Example

President of a Country.

At a given time,

there is only one President.

Everyone refers to the same person.

------------------------------------------------------------

Software Industry Examples

• Database Connection Manager
• Logger
• Configuration Manager
• Cache Manager
• Thread Pool Manager

