Q2. How is Singleton implemented in Java?

Interview Ready Answer

Singleton is implemented using
three components.

------------------------------------------------------------

1. Private Static Instance Variable

Stores the only object
of the class.

private static Singleton instance;

------------------------------------------------------------

2. Private Constructor

Prevents object creation
using the new keyword.

private Singleton(){

}

------------------------------------------------------------

3. Public Static getInstance() Method

Returns the same object every time.

If the object doesn't exist,

it creates it.

public static Singleton getInstance(){

    if(instance==null){

        instance=new Singleton();
    }

    return instance;
}

------------------------------------------------------------

Complete Code

class Singleton{

    private static Singleton instance;

    private Singleton(){

    }

    public static Singleton getInstance(){

        if(instance==null){

            instance=new Singleton();
        }

        return instance;
    }
}

